            {
                "entry_id": "188c374a-09cb-3be1-b256-dd541044fee1",
                "word": "Fletcherite",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "ee2f7e94-aee6-4ad1-9230-7fbb789fe442",
                        "entry_id": "188c374a-09cb-3be1-b256-dd541044fee1",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "Fletcherites"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "60dff7d9-7249-33d1-a069-f3c7656b3229",
                        "entry_id": "188c374a-09cb-3be1-b256-dd541044fee1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A practitioner of Horace Fletcher's theories, especially regarding the extremely thorough chewing of food."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5069e47d-503a-4173-9f8e-f2e6ac084166",
                                "sense_id": "60dff7d9-7249-33d1-a069-f3c7656b3229",
                                "text": "Now I submit that the Fletcherite bowel, which at its fullest is practically empty, and at its most septic is practically microbe-free, approximates so nearly to the condition of the foetal bowel, that if the absorption of undestroyed trypsin is credible in the one case it is credible in the other."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c1cfacab-2106-43ab-844b-68d1cdd0ee6f",
                                "sense_id": "60dff7d9-7249-33d1-a069-f3c7656b3229",
                                "text": "Their contents would have made the weariest Fletcherite drool at the mouth and forget his number of chews."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f1da02e8-a42f-45dc-aa81-5aac96746acc",
                                "sense_id": "60dff7d9-7249-33d1-a069-f3c7656b3229",
                                "text": "The motto of the Fletcherites was “Nature will castigate those who don't masticate.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2c0fd2b0-4fd6-43af-b979-9faa0c61cd84",
                                "sense_id": "60dff7d9-7249-33d1-a069-f3c7656b3229",
                                "text": "It is fascinating to read that any waste generated out of a Fletcherites body will have no offensive odor, be it the digestion ash (excreta), urine or sweat."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
